 The taskbar clock is the clock app's setting, not a second opinion.

 The band formatted its own time from the RTC registers, so a twelve hour
 choice made in the pane reached the pane and nothing else and two clocks on
 one screen disagreed about what time it was. `clk-band-text` is now the one
 builder both call.

 THE LAST ROW IS THE WIRING ROW AND THE REST ARE THE BUILDER. Rows one to five
 ask whether the builder honours the setting, which would stay green on a band
 that never called it, and that is the shape of defect this pane has produced
 three times. `dk-task-clock-w-of` is the taskbar's own width reservation and
 it is derived from the mask, so it moves only if the BAND reads the app's
 setting. It is the narrowest thing in the taskbar that a headless arm can ask.

Section: Test

  cb-ds : Integer -> Integer
  cb-ds (ks) =
    let ds = alloc-zeroed dk-ds-bytes 64
    in let c = poke-32 ds desk-clock-cell ks
    in ds

 A block with a zone and a format, standing in for one the pane has loaded.

  cb-ks : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  cb-ks (cfmt) (mask) =
    let ks = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let a = poke-32 ks clk-cfmt-cell cfmt
    in let b = poke-32 ks clk-dfmt-cell loc-date-dmy
    in let c = clk-set-band ks mask
    in let d = clk-set-zone ks 0
    in ks

  cb-text : Integer, Integer -> Text
  cb-text (cfmt) (mask) = clk-band-text (cb-ks cfmt mask) 13 5 0 7 9 26

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (v) = if v then "yes" else "no"

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let t24 = cb-text loc-clock-24 zone-band-time
    in let t12 = cb-text loc-clock-12 zone-band-time
    in let td = cb-text loc-clock-24 (zone-band-time + zone-band-date)
    in let toff = cb-text loc-clock-24 (zone-band-time + zone-band-offset)
    in let none = cb-text loc-clock-24 0
    in let fresh = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let dflt = clk-band fresh
    in let wt = dk-task-clock-w-of (cb-ds (cb-ks loc-clock-24 zone-band-time))
    in let wall = dk-task-clock-w-of (cb-ds (cb-ks loc-clock-24 zone-band-all))
    in act
      print-line-uni ("24 and 12 hour differ: " & yn (t24 /= t12))
      print-line-uni ("the date adds to it: " & yn (td /= t24 & text-length td > text-length t24))
      print-line-uni ("the offset adds to it: " & yn (toff /= t24 & text-length toff > text-length t24))
      print-line-uni ("an empty mask shows nothing: " & yn (text-length none == 0))
      print-line-uni ("an unwritten block is time only: " & yn (dflt == zone-band-time))
      print-line-uni ("the band reservation follows it: " & yn (wall > wt))
    end
